# Everything below is EXCLUDED FROM THE DEPLOYMENT, not merely blocked by a route.
#
# This matters more than it looks. Vercel applies the filesystem BEFORE rewrites, so a rewrite cannot
# gate a file that exists (their docs say so explicitly). The only version of this that is not a race
# with routing precedence is: the paid bytes are never uploaded, so there is nothing to prefer.
#
# If you add a protected page to PROTECT in server.js / the edge functions, add it here too.
# tests/vercel-entry.js fails if the two lists drift.

# the graded corpus and the paid workspace
task.html
queue.html
onboarding.html
detector.html
trust-safety.html
earnings.html
js/tasks.js
js/detector.js

# the lock screen itself: it is the one page a crawler must not index as free content, and the gate
# serves deploy/gate-fallback.html in its place, so it costs nothing to leave it out
gate.html

# owner-side material that has no business on a public host
data/
tools/
tests/
supabase/
.gitignore
.vercelignore
README.md
ACCESS.md
DEPLOY.md
QUICKSTART.md
